From: Spottedleaf <Spottedleaf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2020 01:49:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf - Optimise non-flush packet sending

Original license: GPL-3.0-only
Original project: https://github.com/PaperMC/Paper
Paper pull request: https://github.com/PaperMC/Paper/pull/10172
Ported from Leaf 26.2 and adapted for Canvas configuration.

Places such as entity tracking make heavy use of packet sending. Scheduling
one Netty task per packet can trigger expensive event-loop wakeups even when
the caller intentionally does not flush yet. Use SingleThreadEventLoop's
lazyExecute for non-flush writes, allowing Netty to process them without a
wakeup for every queued packet.

Canvas additionally guards the optimisation behind an instanceof check so
custom/exotic event loop implementations keep the normal execution path.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
index f518501cb80820e35c4fc81f1c25b9210f985f0c..31dcb2ca151b411d82dc1e0b1e41e8d3dfd65d45 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
@@ -128,6 +128,7 @@ public class Connection extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet<?>> {
     public boolean isPending = true;
     public boolean queueImmunity;
     // Paper end - Optimize network
+    private io.netty.channel.@Nullable SingleThreadEventLoop canvas$eventLoop; // Canvas - optimise packets that are not flushed
 
     public Connection(final PacketFlow receiving) {
         this.receiving = receiving;
@@ -137,6 +138,8 @@ public class Connection extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet<?>> {
     public void channelActive(final ChannelHandlerContext ctx) throws Exception {
         super.channelActive(ctx);
         this.channel = ctx.channel();
+        this.canvas$eventLoop = this.channel.eventLoop() instanceof io.netty.channel.SingleThreadEventLoop eventLoop
+            ? eventLoop : null; // Canvas - optimise packets that are not flushed
         this.address = this.channel.remoteAddress();
         this.preparing = false; // Spigot
         if (this.delayedDisconnect != null) {
@@ -487,6 +490,13 @@ public class Connection extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet<?>> {
         if (this.channel.eventLoop().inEventLoop()) {
             this.doSendPacket(packet, listener, flush);
         } else {
+            // Canvas start - optimise packets that are not flushed; Leaf/Paper-derived
+            if (!flush
+                && this.canvas$eventLoop != null
+                && io.canvasmc.canvas.network.NetworkOptimizationsConfiguration.getInstance().packetSending.optimizeNonFlushPacketSending) {
+                this.canvas$eventLoop.lazyExecute(() -> this.doSendPacket(packet, listener, false));
+            } else
+                // Canvas end - optimise packets that are not flushed
             this.channel.eventLoop().execute(() -> this.doSendPacket(packet, listener, flush));
         }
     }
